        id: 'playwright-setup', title: 'Playwright Setup',
        content: 'Playwright is installed as a development dependency and configured through a playwright.config.ts file. The configuration specifies the test directory, browser projects, and the web server to start before tests run. For Angular applications, point the webServer command to ng serve and set the port to 4200. The baseURL setting lets you navigate to pages using relative paths. The config supports multiple browser projects including Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit, allowing you to test cross-browser compatibility from a single test suite. Enable retries in CI environments to handle transient failures. Set fullyParallel to true to run test files concurrently for faster execution. Configure the reporter to generate HTML reports for debugging failed tests. Install Playwright browsers as a CI step using npx playwright install with deps flag for system dependencies. In your test files, import test and expect from @playwright/test. The test function defines individual test cases, and the page fixture provides a browser page instance. Use page.goto to navigate to your Angular application, and chain assertions with expect to verify page content, element visibility, and URL changes. The test.beforeEach hook sets up common state like navigating to a page before each test runs.'
