        id: 'component-integration', title: 'Component Integration Tests',
        content: 'Component integration tests verify that multiple components work together correctly. Instead of testing a component in isolation with all dependencies mocked, you import its actual child components and test the real interactions. Configure TestBed with the parent component and its child components in the imports array. Provide real or mock services depending on what you want to verify. For example, a user list component that renders user card children can import both components and verify that the list passes data to each card correctly. Test that actions in child components propagate to the parent. When a user clicks delete on a card, verify the parent component receives the event and updates its list. Integration tests catch issues like mismatched input types, missing event bindings, and incorrect data transformations between components. They are slower than unit tests but provide higher confidence that your component tree works as a cohesive unit. Focus integration tests on critical user workflows and component boundaries where data flows between components. Use them to verify that your component composition is correct and that parent-child communication works as expected.'
