        id: 'test-utilities', title: 'Shared Test Utilities',
        content: 'Shared test utilities reduce duplication and enforce consistency across your test suite. Create helper functions for common operations like creating component fixtures, querying DOM elements, and waiting for async operations. A createComponent helper can wrap the standard TestBed setup and return a configured fixture. DOM query helpers like getElement and getAllElements provide typed access to rendered elements without repetitive casting. Reusable mock data files define fixtures for common entities like users, products, or orders. Centralizing mock data ensures consistency across tests and makes it easy to update when the data model changes. Export constants for mock API responses, error objects, and configuration values. Create base TestBed configurations that include common providers like HTTP client, router, and animations. Spread these configurations into individual test modules to reduce boilerplate. For HTTP testing, create a helper that sets up HttpTestingController and provides functions for flushing mock responses. Document each utility with JSDoc comments explaining its purpose and parameters. Organize utilities by domain, placing component helpers in one file, service helpers in another, and shared mock data in a separate file. This organization makes utilities easy to discover and maintain as your test suite grows.'
