        content: 'Lighthouse CI automates performance auditing in your continuous integration pipeline. Install it as a development dependency and create a configuration file that specifies which pages to audit and what score thresholds to enforce. The collect section configures how Lighthouse runs your application. Point startServerCommand to ng serve and set numberOfRuns to 3 for statistically meaningful results. Define the URLs to test, including your homepage and critical routes. The assert section defines performance budgets. Set minimum scores for performance, accessibility, best practices, and SEO categories. Configure numeric thresholds for specific metrics like First Contentful Paint under 2000 milliseconds, Largest Contentful Paint under 2500 milliseconds, and Cumulative Layout Shift under 0.1. The upload section sends results to a Lighthouse CI server for tracking over time. In GitHub Actions, add a step that runs npx lhci autorun after your build completes. Lighthouse CI will fail the build if any assertions fail, preventing performance regressions from reaching production. Track performance scores across builds to identify trends and catch gradual degradation. Review Lighthouse reports for specific recommendations like image optimization, code splitting, and render-blocking resources.'
